Embedded React: let rounded images be host layers.

Modified from Embedded React (Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Cory Lamming) at the
revision pinned in dependencies.lock.json, after the patches listed before this
one there. Changed files: engine/include/er_scene.h, engine/scene/compositor.c
and engine/tests/rendering/test_layers.c.

A rounded image was never a layer, so a screen of rounded posters rescaled every
poster on the CPU whenever a card around it repainted. A rounded image at full
opacity now qualifies: the rasterizer draws only the square of its radius at
each rounded corner, anti-aliased edge and all, and clears the rest of the box.
ERLayer carries the clamped radii, and the host leaves those squares to the
framebuffer. A rounded layer never covers a translucent one, whose rule needs
an opaque rect beneath it. An image scrolled entirely out of view is no longer
a candidate, so it cannot take an ERUI_MAX_LAYERS slot from one in view.
test_layers checks rounded layers over a layer and over a rounded panel against
the rasterized scene.

